--- body ---
## Context
Roar's attribution capture for PR #1853 refused (2026-10-28, journal
`memory/journal/2026/2026-10-28-readme-pr1853-f1-notes-gap.md`). One gaze run (Pi,
padme/qwen3.8-flash-next-iq3_s) typed one Codex seat twice, under two names:
- attribution file -> PR body: `seat=consistency` (the plan item), `model=openai/gpt-6-luna`;
- result comment: `seat: code-reviewer` (the `--role` profile), `model=gpt-6-luna`.
`attribution_record.py` `seat_lines()` joins the two by exact seat name, so the body seat was unmatched
and the comment seat was derived anew; the derived line then failed the provider-qualified model check.

Two defects:
1. Proximate: `skills/gaze/references/output.md` template `seat: <role>` is ambiguous (plan item name or
   `--role` profile), and the identity is hand-typed in two places with no check until roar.
2. Latent: the derive path copies the worker header's model, which is the bare route pin
   (`skills/route/grid.json` stores `gpt-6-luna`; `scripts/gaze_seat.py` writes `worker: model=<pin>`),
   while `attribution_record.py` requires `provider/model`. Any unmatched seat fails capture.

## Design (option C)
- `gaze_close.py` builds every `seat:` line of the posted result and every `reviewer: step=review` line of
  the attribution append from the plan's item names and each report's launcher-set `worker:` header
  (model, family, runtime, door) plus the seat status files. The model types neither.
- One name per seat: the plan item name, used in the plan, roster, `seat:` line and `seat=` field.
- The model id is provider-qualified at that one point (from the header's family/runtime, or the grid
  row's provider), so derived and appended lines pass `attribution_record.py` strict identity.
- The model still writes `finding:` lines (path:line, adopted) in the attribution file, keyed by seat name;
  `gaze_close.py` refuses to post when a finding names a seat absent from the plan.
- Template text in `output.md` and gaze `SKILL.md` § Attribution changes to say the lines are generated.

## Imagine annotation (raid 2026-10-28)
Ordered after 1301 (PR #1858), which rewrites gaze_close.py, attribution_record.py, output.md, gaze SKILL.md,
test_gaze_close.py and test_attribution_seats.py, and already fixes defect 2 (seat_lines prefixes a bare model with
the seat family). Simplest path within option C:
- one `identities(panel)` in `scripts/seat_clock.py` (beside `roster`, sharing `assess`'s parse of
  `<panel>/manifest.txt`, `<panel>/<name>.md` headers and `.md.status`), used by plan-check and gaze_close;
- gaze_close fills a `{{seats}}` placeholder (like `{{plan_check}}`) with the generated `seat:` lines;
- `--seats-pr` (post-1301) derives the body `reviewer:` lines from them; the attribution file carries only
  `finding:` lines; gaze_close refuses (non-zero, nothing posted) on a finding naming a seat absent from the manifest.

## Blind-Spot constraints (raid 2026-10-28)
1. Subagent-door seats type their own `worker:` header (profiles/code-reviewer/PROFILE.md:28,
   prose-reviewer:23; panel.md subagent door). Take model from the manifest pin and runtime from the session,
   or label the line self-reported; never present a seat-typed header as launcher-derived. Fixture required.
2. A failed or no-report seat has no header; a derived `model=not observed` is a capture failure in
   seat_lines unless masked evidence is given. Choose the rule against the attribution contract
   (conception/2026-10-02-reviewer-attribution-design.md) so a failed seat never blocks capture; fixture required.
3. The panel lives in the review worktree, removed by cleanup(): compute identities before cleanup, next to
   plan_check_line (pr/1858 gaze_close.py:299 vs :316), and carry them into the blocked-cleanup ESCALATE answer.
4. Seat names join past records (attribution_query.py:21 keys on seat; roar capture.md asks stable names):
   plan item names carry no round suffix; check existing journal seat names before fixing the rule.
5. Provider qualification reuses `billed_provider()` (scripts/gaze_seat.py:219), not a family-string rule;
   fixture for a Pi any-provider seat.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] A test replays the #1853 shape (plan item `consistency`, `--role code-reviewer`, bare pin `gpt-6-luna`): gaze_close emits one name and a provider-qualified model (qualification already provided by 1301; kept as a regression assertion), and `attribution_record.py --seats-pr` then captures with no failure.
- [ ] Neither `output.md` nor gaze `SKILL.md` asks the model to type `seat:` or `reviewer:` identity lines.
- [ ] `gaze_close.py` refuses (non-zero, nothing posted) when a `finding:` names a seat not in the plan; test covers it.
- [ ] Self seats (no worker header) still produce a valid line from the session's own identity, as today.
- [ ] `make check` passes.
